{"4024980": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "MIA: Memory Fragments", "steam_appid": 4024980, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>You didn’t return to remember.</strong></h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>You returned to survive what you forgot.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In <i><strong>MIA: Memory Fragments</strong></i>, moving forward means stepping back into moments you don’t fully remember. Familiar places repeat, conversations feel incomplete, and the world reacts when you get too close to the truth.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Some paths open when you face what happened. <br>Others awaken something that wants you to stop digging.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >   </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Reconstruct the story and uncover the truth</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are no long explanations.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Understanding comes from revisiting shared moments, noticing what repeats, and confronting the fragments that refuse to stay hidden.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/853afea37e4781df6e12ccf70b54a5b8.poster.avif?t=1770107260\" width=780 height=320 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/853afea37e4781df6e12ccf70b54a5b8.webm?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/853afea37e4781df6e12ccf70b54a5b8.mp4?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span> </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Escape When Memory Turns Hostile</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Not all memories want to be uncovered.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When MIA’s darkest side appears, exploration turns into survival. Run, hide, and escape as the rules of the world break.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/e57dd8befa467fd82a6601657af63c33.poster.avif?t=1770107260\" width=780 height=320 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/e57dd8befa467fd82a6601657af63c33.webm?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/e57dd8befa467fd82a6601657af63c33.mp4?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Explore to Move Forward</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore interconnected environments and observe your surroundings carefully.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Progress by navigating spaces, examining details, and interacting with key elements that allow you to move deeper into the memory.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/87ee1c6ed1bae9d0911d9fded598ca3b.poster.avif?t=1770107260\" width=780 height=320 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/87ee1c6ed1bae9d0911d9fded598ca3b.webm?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/87ee1c6ed1bae9d0911d9fded598ca3b.mp4?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Overcome Blocked Paths</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Progress is often shaped by interaction.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At certain moments, you can engage with specific elements through short challenges that add variety, restore missing fragments, and let you move forward.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/b7603e70175a0bb9e9013307a5616329.poster.avif?t=1770107260\" width=780 height=320 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/b7603e70175a0bb9e9013307a5616329.webm?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/b7603e70175a0bb9e9013307a5616329.mp4?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The deeper you go, the harder it becomes to tell truth from denial.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Face the memories… or stay trapped inside them forever.</strong></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Add MIA to your wishlist!</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p>", "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>You didn’t return to remember.</strong></h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>You returned to survive what you forgot.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In <i><strong>MIA: Memory Fragments</strong></i>, moving forward means stepping back into moments you don’t fully remember. Familiar places repeat, conversations feel incomplete, and the world reacts when you get too close to the truth.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Some paths open when you face what happened. <br>Others awaken something that wants you to stop digging.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >   </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Reconstruct the story and uncover the truth</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are no long explanations.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Understanding comes from revisiting shared moments, noticing what repeats, and confronting the fragments that refuse to stay hidden.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/853afea37e4781df6e12ccf70b54a5b8.poster.avif?t=1770107260\" width=780 height=320 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/853afea37e4781df6e12ccf70b54a5b8.webm?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/853afea37e4781df6e12ccf70b54a5b8.mp4?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span> </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Escape When Memory Turns Hostile</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Not all memories want to be uncovered.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When MIA’s darkest side appears, exploration turns into survival. Run, hide, and escape as the rules of the world break.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/e57dd8befa467fd82a6601657af63c33.poster.avif?t=1770107260\" width=780 height=320 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/e57dd8befa467fd82a6601657af63c33.webm?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/e57dd8befa467fd82a6601657af63c33.mp4?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Explore to Move Forward</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore interconnected environments and observe your surroundings carefully.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Progress by navigating spaces, examining details, and interacting with key elements that allow you to move deeper into the memory.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/87ee1c6ed1bae9d0911d9fded598ca3b.poster.avif?t=1770107260\" width=780 height=320 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/87ee1c6ed1bae9d0911d9fded598ca3b.webm?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/87ee1c6ed1bae9d0911d9fded598ca3b.mp4?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Overcome Blocked Paths</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Progress is often shaped by interaction.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At certain moments, you can engage with specific elements through short challenges that add variety, restore missing fragments, and let you move forward.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/b7603e70175a0bb9e9013307a5616329.poster.avif?t=1770107260\" width=780 height=320 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/b7603e70175a0bb9e9013307a5616329.webm?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/extras/b7603e70175a0bb9e9013307a5616329.mp4?t=1770107260\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The deeper you go, the harder it becomes to tell truth from denial.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Face the memories… or stay trapped inside them forever.</strong></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Add MIA to your wishlist!</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p>", "short_description": "MIA: Memory Fragments is a story-driven psychological horror adventure where you explore fractured memories, interact with the environment to progress, uncover the story through the world, and escape from MIA’s darkest side. Survive the memories… or remain trapped forever in the past.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, Spanish - Spain<strong>*</strong>, Korean, Japanese<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/b5b475d67d5cfe694c88e34c2ac7eec2c0a3a9bb/header.jpg?t=1770107260", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/1af8968d4560245a3ff7b0ff5d7f5115fa764a42/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1770107260", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4024980/1af8968d4560245a3ff7b0ff5d7f5115fa764a42/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1770107260", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10/11<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i5-2300 @ 2,80 GHz, AMD FX 8120 @ 3.1 GHz<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 6 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> NVIDIA GT 630 / 650m, AMD Radeon HD6570 or equivalent<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 10<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 2 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong>  100% DirectX 9.0c compatible sound card</li></ul>", "recommended": "<